  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>The back of this shield is rough bark, and the front is smooth heartwood with rings too many to count. Set down on bare earth, it leans toward the nearest water.</p><p>You have a +3 bonus to Armor Class while you wield this shield.</p><p><strong>Plant the Wall.</strong> Once per day, as an action, you drive the shield's point into the ground and cast @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplWallofThor]{Wall of Thorns} (save DC 20) without Concentration; the wall lasts for 10 minutes or until you pull the shield free. The shield regains this power at dawn.</p><p><strong>What Grows After.</strong> Left planted overnight, the shield takes root for good and cannot be pulled free. A grove grows there within a year, and its trees will tell whoever planted the shield everything that has passed beneath them.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
